From: Banks Troutman <banks.troutman@oxos.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: tegra210-i2s: nvidia,audio-channels/sample-size DT overrides

Read nvidia,audio-channels and nvidia,sample-size from the I2S DT node at
probe and apply them as the channel-count / sample-format overrides. Without
this the DPCM codec-to-codec link negotiates 2ch/S16 and the I2S5 BCLK/LRCK
framing is wrong for an 8ch/32-bit TDM codec (CS42448).

bit_count is intentionally left to the stock computation, which derives BCLK
from the *requested* params: srate * channels * sample_size = 48000*8*32 =
12_288_000, giving bit_count = 256-1 = 255 (one full 8x32 frame).

HARDWARE-PROVEN ROOT CAUSE (do not "fix" by reading the real clock):
A prior revision read the *actual* BCLK back with clk_get_rate() and used it
for bit_count. The Tegra PLLA produces 12_287_996 Hz (not 12_288_000), so the
integer divide 12287996/48000 = 255 yielded bit_count 254 — one bit short per
frame. That corrupted the LAST TDM slot only (slot 7 aliased onto DAC1/AOUT2,
audible as sharp/loud distortion; slots 0-6 fine). Verified on A203 by per-slot
scope + ear mapping. Keep the computed rate, and force the BPMP i2s5 clock to
256xFs externally via i2s5-clock-fix.service — the BPMP otherwise rounds
clk_set_rate(12288000) UP to 24.576 MHz (512xFs), which the codec cannot frame.

---
--- a/sound/soc/tegra/tegra210_i2s.c
+++ b/sound/soc/tegra/tegra210_i2s.c
@@ -1240,6 +1240,20 @@

 	regcache_cache_only(i2s->regmap, true);

+	{
+		unsigned int v;
+		if (of_property_read_u32(dev->of_node, "nvidia,audio-channels", &v) == 0) {
+			i2s->audio_ch_override[I2S_RX_PATH] = v;
+			i2s->audio_ch_override[I2S_TX_PATH] = v;
+			i2s->client_ch_override = v;
+		}
+		if (of_property_read_u32(dev->of_node, "nvidia,sample-size", &v) == 0) {
+			i2s->audio_fmt_override[I2S_RX_PATH] = (v == 32) ? 2 : 1;
+			i2s->audio_fmt_override[I2S_TX_PATH] = (v == 32) ? 2 : 1;
+			i2s->client_fmt_override = (v == 32) ? 2 : 1;
+		}
+	}
+
 	err = devm_snd_soc_register_component(dev, &tegra210_i2s_cmpnt,
 					      tegra210_i2s_dais,
 					      ARRAY_SIZE(tegra210_i2s_dais));
